Firefox add-on: Firefox Multi-Account Containers (@testpilot-containers)

configure-gnome-desktop.sh builds the add-on with ../build-addon.py from the release which "release" pins, the file
addons.mozilla.org serves for version 8.4.0 with the SHA-256 it publishes for it, applies the patches listed in
"series" and installs the result into /usr/lib/firefox-addons/extensions, Firefox's application directory for add-ons
on Ubuntu. Ubuntu's Firefox is built with MOZ_UNSIGNED_APP_SCOPE, so it loads add-ons from there without a signature,
which it requires everywhere else, and only root can write there. The add-on keeps its ID, and with it its data, such
as the site assignments of its containers.

Firefox never updates an add-on in that directory, so a new release of the add-on needs a new pin in "release". The
daily run of rebuild-patched-packages.sh asks addons.mozilla.org for the current release, and when it is not the
pinned one, tries the patches on it and mails the outcome once, with the new lines for "release" when they apply, see
../check-addon-release.py. A copy installed from addons.mozilla.org into a profile takes precedence over the add-on
there, and configure-gnome-desktop.sh reports such a copy. Deleting its file from the profile's extensions directory
while Firefox is not running activates the add-on from the application directory with the same data, while removing
the add-on in Firefox's add-on manager deletes its data.

reopen-in-window-of-tab.patch
    The add-on reopens a page assigned to a container in a new tab of that container, and removes the tab it replaces
    when that tab was new. It creates the new tab in the window which had the focus last, at the index the tab it
    replaces has in its own window, and removes that tab at once. When Firefox opens a link from another application in
    a new window while another window has the focus, as during a start which restores the session, the link becomes a
    tab of that other window, and its own window closes with its only tab. When the tab it replaces stays, Firefox
    refuses to create the new tab, whose opener that tab is, in another window, so the page does not open at all. This
    is https://github.com/mozilla/multi-account-containers/issues/2000.

    The patch creates the new tab in the window of the tab it replaces, and removes that tab only once the new one
    exists. It is a commit of the add-on's repository, against 8.4.0, whose main branch has the same code, and changes
    the add-on's tests too, so that they check the window and wait for the removal. Only its changes below src/ apply to
    the release. The add-on's tests pass with it (npm ci --legacy-peer-deps, then npx mocha 'test/**/*.test.js').

    tests/firefox/test_container_tab_window.py checks it in Firefox, see tests/firefox/README. The patch is proposed
    upstream as https://github.com/mozilla/multi-account-containers/pull/2957. Drop it once a release of the add-on
    includes the fix.
